  ('account', '1. No account to close', '<p>Photo Games currently has no registration, sign-in, or server accounts. You can delete photos and game data directly on your device without closing an account. The developer holds no app account or uploaded photos.</p>'),
  ('photos', '2. Delete a photo or pack', '<ol><li>Open <strong>Photo packs → Manage my photo packs</strong> and choose a pack.</li><li>Tap a photo and choose <strong>Delete photo from app</strong>, or select <strong>Delete photo pack</strong>.</li><li>Confirm the deletion. Copies inside the app are removed; original photos in your gallery are kept.</li></ol>'),
  ('records', '3. Reset game records', '<p>From Home, choose <strong>Settings → Reset game records → Delete records</strong>. This removes records and record badges. <strong>Unlocked levels, stars, and photo packs remain.</strong> Use the full deletion steps below to remove all progress.</p>'),
  ('all', '4. Delete all app data', '<ol><li>In Android, open <strong>Settings → Apps → 사진게임 → Storage</strong>.</li><li>Choose <strong>Clear data</strong> or <strong>Clear storage</strong> and confirm, or uninstall the app. Menu names vary by device.</li><li>This removes photo copies, pack names, levels, stars, records, solo/together/challenge state, participant names, and settings held in the app.</li></ol><div class="callout"><strong>Clearing the cache alone does not delete all app data.</strong><p>There is no cloud backup or restore feature, so progress cannot be restored after full deletion.</p></div>'),
  ('outside', '5. Data managed elsewhere', '<p>Original gallery photos, exported result cards, and challenge codes or messages sent to friends are not removed by clearing app data. Manage them in the gallery, file manager, or sharing service. Recipients may retain files and messages already sent to them.</p>'),
